{"event": "artifact", "agent": "documentation", "file": "README.md", "content": "# Bank Account\n\nA simple Python class `BankAccount` that allows you to manage a bank account with basic operations like deposits, withdrawals, and checking the balance.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe `BankAccount` class provides a straightforward way to handle bank account transactions without any user interface. It ensures that all transactions are valid and updates the account balance accordingly.\n\n## API\n\n### Class: `BankAccount`\n\n#### Attributes:\n- `owner`: The name of the account holder.\n- `balance`: The current balance in the account.\n\n#### Methods:\n- `__init__(self, owner, initial_balance=0)`: Initializes a new bank account with an owner and an optional initial balance. Raises a `ValueError` if the initial balance is negative.\n  \n- `deposit(self, amount)`: Deposits a specified amount into the account. Raises a `ValueError` if the amount is less than or equal to zero. Returns the updated balance.\n\n- `withdraw(self, amount)`: Withdraws a specified amount from the account. Raises a `ValueError` if the amount is less than or equal to zero or exceeds the available balance. Returns the updated balance.\n\n- `get_balance(self)`: Returns the current balance of the account.\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom app import BankAccount\n\n# Create a new bank account\naccount = BankAccount(\"John Doe\", 100)\n\n# Deposit money\nprint(account.deposit(50))  # Output: 150\n\n# Withdraw money\nprint(account.withdraw(20))  # Output: 130\n\n# Check balance\nprint(account.get_balance())  # Output: 130\n```\n\n## Running Tests\n\nTo ensure the functionality works as expected, you can run the tests using `pytest`. Make sure you have `pytest` installed:\n\n```sh\npip install pytest\n```\n\nThen, run the tests:\n\n```sh\npytest test_app.py\n```\n\nThis will execute the tests defined in `test_app.py`, which should cover the main functionalities of the `BankAccount` class."}
